**How to implement.** A user-supplied Zemax glass catalogue (`.agf`, as Schott, Ohara, Hoya and CDGM publish theirs) is read into user materials, each glass's dispersion formula rewritten as the refractiveindex.info formula of the same equation and lowered by MaterialImport's existing lowering, so no second formula engine exists (001 §D 'User-supplied glass catalogues (Schott / Ohara / Hoya / CDGM AGF): import only, never bundle'; the S13.2 brief 'Their formula coefficients are lowered through MaterialImport's existing formula lowering'; .spec-md §3.19; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). Nothing is bundled: the reader reads a text the user gives. The AGF equations, λ in µm and C1 … Cn the `CD` coefficients in order, as OpticSim.jl evaluates them (`src/GlassCat/utilities.jl`, verified 2026-11-04): 1 Schott n² = C1 + C2λ² + C3λ⁻² + C4λ⁻⁴ + C5λ⁻⁶ + C6λ⁻⁸; 2 Sellmeier 1 n² = 1 + C1λ²/(λ²−C2) + C3λ²/(λ²−C4) + C5λ²/(λ²−C6); 3 Herzberger n = C1 + C2L + C3L² + C4λ² + C5λ⁴ + C6λ⁶, L = 1/(λ²−0.028); 4 Sellmeier 2 n² = 1 + C1 + C2λ²/(λ²−C3²) + C4λ²/(λ²−C5²); 5 Conrady n = C1 + C2/λ + C3/λ^3.5; 6 Sellmeier 3, formula 2 with a fourth term C7λ²/(λ²−C8); 7 Handbook of Optics 1 n² = C1 + C2/(λ²−C3) − C4λ²; 8 Handbook of Optics 2 n² = C1 + C2λ²/(λ²−C3) − C4λ²; 9 Sellmeier 4 n² = C1 + C2λ²/(λ²−C3) + C4λ²/(λ²−C5); 10 Extended n² = formula 1 + C7λ⁻¹⁰ + C8λ⁻¹²; 11 Sellmeier 5, formula 2 over five terms C1 … C10; 12 Extended 2 n² = formula 1 + C7λ⁴ + C8λ⁶; 13 Extended 3 n² = C1 + C2λ² + C3λ⁴ + C4λ⁻² + C5λ⁻⁴ + C6λ⁻⁶ + C7λ⁻⁸ + C8λ⁻¹⁰ + C9λ⁻¹². Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`: (1) `AgfFormulaNumber of int` with `.value` and `member this.family : string` (`Schott`, `Sellmeier 1`, `Herzberger`, `Sellmeier 2`, `Conrady`, `Sellmeier 3`, `Handbook of Optics 1`, `Handbook of Optics 2`, `Sellmeier 4`, `Extended`, `Sellmeier 5`, `Extended 2`, `Extended 3`, or `AGF formula <n>`). `type AgfFormulaNumber with member this.riiFormOf (c : float array) : Result<RiiFormulaNumber * float array, ImportError>` rewrites a glass's coefficients (absent ones zero) as the refractiveindex.info page of the same equation (`RiiFormulaNumber`, `MaterialImport.fs:30`): 1 is formula 3 `[C1; C2; 2; C3; −2; C4; −4; C5; −6; C6; −8]`; 2, 6 and 11 are formula 2 `[0; C1; C2; …]` over three, four and five pairs; 3 is formula 7 `[C1 … C6]`; 4 is formula 1 `[C1; C2; C3; C4; C5]` (formula 1 squares its resonances); 5 is formula 5 `[C1; C2; −1; C3; −3.5]`; 7 is formula 4 `[C1; C2; 0; C3; 1; 0; 0; 0; 0; −C4; 2]` and 8 formula 4 `[C1; C2; 2; C3; 1; 0; 0; 0; 0; −C4; 2]`; 9 is formula 2 `[C1 − 1; C2; C3; C4; C5]`; 10, 12 and 13 are formula 3 over their powers in order; any other number is `MalformedSourceFileErr` naming it. Each pair is the equation term for term, so no number is approximated. (2) `GlassCatalogueText of string` with `.value`; `static member ofBytes (bytes : byte[]) : GlassCatalogueText` decodes a UTF-16 little-endian (`FF FE`) or big-endian (`FE FF`) byte-order mark as that encoding, a UTF-8 mark as UTF-8, and otherwise UTF-16 little-endian when one of the first two bytes is zero and UTF-8 when none is, as Zemax writes its catalogues in either. `type GlassCatalogueText with member this.importGlasses : Result<MaterialEntry list, ImportError>`: lines (`\r\n` as `\n`) whose first token is `NM` open a glass: its second token is the name and its third the formula number, read as an integer or as a real with no fraction (`2.0`); `CD` gives its coefficients and `LD` its range (two numbers, µm, through `toWaveLength Micrometer`, as the page range is, `MaterialImport.fs:142`; a glass without `LD` takes the zero nominal interval as a page without a range does); a line starting with `!` and every other keyword (`CC`, `GC`, `ED`, `TD`, `OD`, `IT` …) are read past. Each glass is `riiFormOf`, then `lowerFormulaAxis` (`MaterialImport.fs:438`, unchanged), then the formula import's entry assembly (`entryOfAxis`, `MaterialImport.fs:455`, which files it under `CategoryIds.glass`) named by the glass and described `Imported <family> glass (AGF formula <n>).`, in file order. A glass that does not lower (Conrady's λ^3.5, which the lowering refuses as no finite term sum, `MaterialImport.fs:294`) or does not read makes the whole text `MalformedSourceFileErr` naming every such glass with its reason, one per line, so nothing imports silently in part; a text without a glass is `NoDataErr`; every .NET call that throws is caught and answered `MalformedSourceFileErr`. No transmission, thermal or price data, no partial import and no option is added. (3) Fixture: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/test-glasses.agf`, a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `fixtures/ptb-Co.txt`'s with no comment, ASCII, test-local values (not a vendor's): a `CC` line, then `TEST-S1` (formula 2, `CD 1.04 0.006 0.23 0.02 1.01 103.6 0 0 0 0`, `LD 0.3 2.5`, with `GC`, `ED`, `TD`, `OD` and `IT` lines), `TEST-SCHOTT` (formula `1.0`, six coefficients, `LD 0.36 1.5`) and `TEST-HERZ` (formula 3, six coefficients, no `LD`). (4) Tests, in `MaterialImportTests`: `a glass catalogue's glasses lower through MaterialImport's formulas to the AGF equations`: the fixture's three glasses, in order and named so, each match at 0.4, 0.5876 and 1.0 µm, within 1e-12, n² (or n) of its AGF equation the fact evaluates from the fixture's coefficients; and test-local glasses of formulas 4, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 and 13 do so at 0.5876 µm. `a glass catalogue reads in UTF-8 or UTF-16 and takes each glass's wavelength range`: `TEST-S1`'s interval is 0.3 to 2.5 µm and `TEST-HERZ`'s the zero nominal one; the fixture's text encoded UTF-16 little-endian with and without its mark, and UTF-8 with its mark, reads the same three glasses. `a glass catalogue with a glass no formula lowers, or with no glass, is refused`: a test-local text holding a Conrady glass and a formula-14 glass beside `TEST-S1` answers `MalformedSourceFileErr` naming both; a `CC` line alone answers `NoDataErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the reader lands, `GlassCatalogueText.importGlasses` MUST read an AGF catalogue in UTF-8 or UTF-16 into one user glass per `NM` block, each formula rewritten as the refractiveindex.info formula of the same equation and lowered by `lowerFormulaAxis`, refusing the whole text when a glass does not lower; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a glass catalogue's glasses lower through MaterialImport's formulas to the AGF equations`, `a glass catalogue reads in UTF-8 or UTF-16 and takes each glass's wavelength range` and `a glass catalogue with a glass no formula lowers, or with no glass, is refused`, the count rising by 3; kit-acceptance MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with AT-1 and AT-2 expectations and tolerances unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
